https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132858794,imgsize-1069850.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Biodiversity boosts forest growth; loss could cut gains 17% by 2050]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132858357.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-tracked-global-forest-photosynthesis-for-20-years-and-found-species-rich-forests-improved-faster-biodiversity-loss-could-reduce-the-trend-by-up-to-17-by-2050/articleshow/132858357.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-tracked-global-forest-photosynthesis-for-20-years-and-found-species-rich-forests-improved-faster-biodiversity-loss-could-reduce-the-trend-by-up-to-17-by-2050/articleshow/132858357.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-04T16:32:42+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132858524,imgsize-398129.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[World's oldest amber has been found in China, and it is 65 million years older than expected]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132851769.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a remarkable discovery, scientists uncovered ancient amber specimens in China that are approximately 385 million years old. This significant find pushes the amber fossil record back by an impressive sixty-five million years. It indicates that early vascular plants may have developed advanced resin-producing capabilities, which could have provided a defensive advantage against wildfires and fungal diseases. The research advances our understanding of plant resilience during the Devonian era.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/china/worlds-oldest-amber-has-been-found-in-china-and-it-is-65-million-years-older-than-expected/articleshow/132851769.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/china/worlds-oldest-amber-has-been-found-in-china-and-it-is-65-million-years-older-than-expected/articleshow/132851769.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-04T14:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132851769,imgsize-204059.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Long before GPS, Polynesian sailors crossed the Pacific by reading stars, waves, winds, birds and clouds]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132851511.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/long-before-gps-polynesian-sailors-crossed-the-pacific-by-reading-stars-waves-winds-birds-and-clouds/articleshow/132851511.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/long-before-gps-polynesian-sailors-crossed-the-pacific-by-reading-stars-waves-winds-birds-and-clouds/articleshow/132851511.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-04T13:45:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132851628,imgsize-1321195.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Ancient Roman women left more than 120 inscriptions inside a hidden cave in Spain dedicated to a mysterious goddess]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132855196.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/ancient-roman-women-left-more-than-120-inscriptions-inside-a-hidden-cave-in-spain-dedicated-to-a-mysterious-goddess/articleshow/132855196.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/ancient-roman-women-left-more-than-120-inscriptions-inside-a-hidden-cave-in-spain-dedicated-to-a-mysterious-goddess/articleshow/132855196.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-04T15:09:29+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132855431,imgsize-1836191.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[How Felix Dennis launched a 10 million-tree vision to restore England's woodlands]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132855555.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Felix Dennis began planting a small wood in 1996, which grew into the Heart of England Forest. This project aimed to restore native broadleaf trees across South Warwickshire. The charity was established in 2003 to continue purchasing and planting land. Dennis envisioned 25,000 acres of woodland open to the public. After his death in 2014, the forest has expanded significantly.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/how-british-publisher-felix-dennis-responded-to-englands-centuries-of-woodland-lohow-british-publisher-felix-dennis-responded-to-englands-centuries-of-woodland-loss-with-a-vision-of-planting-10-million-trees-in-1996-ss-with-a-vision-of-planting-10-million-trees-in-1996/articleshow/132855555.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/how-british-publisher-felix-dennis-responded-to-englands-centuries-of-woodland-lohow-british-publisher-felix-dennis-responded-to-englands-centuries-of-woodland-loss-with-a-vision-of-planting-10-million-trees-in-1996-ss-with-a-vision-of-planting-10-million-trees-in-1996/articleshow/132855555.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-04T15:45:00+05:30</pubDate