-canadian-town-are-finally-being-removed-after-20-years-of-unbearable-stench/articleshow/132857966.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-04T16:26:48+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132858182,imgsize-1742503.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Andrew Tate's lawyer warns Trump of political fallout if he doesn't help jailed influencer in UK extradition case]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132855695.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/andrew-tates-lawyer-warns-trump-of-political-fallout-if-he-doesnt-help-jailed-influencer-in-uk-extradition-case/articleshow/132855695.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/andrew-tates-lawyer-warns-trump-of-political-fallout-if-he-doesnt-help-jailed-influencer-in-uk-extradition-case/articleshow/132855695.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-04T15:57:40+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132855695,imgsize-100661.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Quote of the day by Princess Diana: "Don't call me an icon. I'm just a mother trying to…"]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132857129.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/quote-of-the-day-by-princess-diana-dont-call-me-an-icon-im-just-a-mother-trying-to-a-timeless-lesson-on-humility-compassion-and-leading-through-kindness/articleshow/132857129.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/quote-of-the-day-by-princess-diana-dont-call-me-an-icon-im-just-a-mother-trying-to-a-timeless-lesson-on-humility-compassion-and-leading-through-kindness/articleshow/132857129.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-04T16:00:18+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132857129,imgsize-51010.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Scientists discover four dangerous fish bacteria in Brazil for the first time; one has jumped to a new host species]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132856374.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[For the first time, Brazil faces a significant challenge as bacteria previously exclusive to Asia and the USA have been identified within its borders. These bacteria, known to cause columnaris disease, pose an acute risk to the thriving aquaculture sector. Researchers have isolated four species from the Flavobacterium genus, which can infect both Nile tilapia and indigenous fish species.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-discover-four-dangerous-fish-bacteria-in-brazil-for-the-first-time-one-has-jumped-to-a-new-host-species/articleshow/132856374.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-discover-four-dangerous-fish-bacteria-in-brazil-for-the-first-time-one-has-jumped-to-a-new-host-species/articleshow/132856374.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-04T15:38:42+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132856374,imgsize-153770.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Scientists warn Earth could hit the 1.5°C climate limit sooner than expected]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132855214.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Global warming has significantly accelerated, with the past decade warming faster than any comparable period. Researchers removed natural climate fluctuations to reveal this underlying warming trend. Five major global temperature datasets confirm this acceleration with high statistical confidence. This observed increase suggests the world may approach key climate thresholds sooner. The long-term trend could cross the Paris Agreement's 1.5°C limit before this decade ends.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-say-global-warming-is-accelerating-heres-why-the-world-could-reach-the-1-5c-climate-limit-sooner-than-expected/articleshow/132855214.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-say-global-warming-is-accelerating-heres-why-the-world-could-reach-the-1-5c-climate-limit-sooner-than-expected/articleshow/132855214.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-04T15:08:57+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132855214,imgsize-145050.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Iran won't escalate tensions but will defend itself, says Pezeshkian amid Trump's warning]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132855001.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Iran states it will defend its security while the US president claims a last chance for a deal. Conflicting reports emerge regarding ongoing negotiations between Iran and the United States. Shipping activity through the Strait of Hormuz remains subdued amid these diplomatic claims. Iran's IRGC reportedly launched a drone attack on a US military base in Kuwait. Tehran also prepared retaliatory strikes on Ukraine after a vessel incident.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/iran-wont-escalate-tensions-but-will-defend-itself-says-pezeshkian-as-donald-trump-claims-tehran-has-last-chance/articleshow/132855001.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/iran-wont-escalate-tensions-but-will-defend-itself-says-pezeshkian-as-donald-trump-claims-tehran-has-last-chance/articleshow/132855001.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-04T15:07:53+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yashasvi Vasistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132855750,imgsize-700102.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Scientists in Iceland are turning carbon dioxide into stone by injecting it into volcanic rock, and it could redefine the fight against climate change]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132852635.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-in-iceland-are-turning-carbon-dioxide-into-stone-by-injecting-it-into-volcanic-rock-and-it-could-redefine-the-fight-against-climate-change/articleshow/132852635.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-in-iceland-are-turning-carbon-dioxide-into-stone-by-injecting-it-into-volcanic-rock-and-it-could-redefine-the-fight-against-climate-change/articleshow/132852635.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-04T13:54:56+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132852902,imgsize-1015443.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Mark Zuckerberg's wife invested $125 million in a school for the disadvantaged; now she is closing it to focus on AI]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132850734.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The Primary School, offering tuition-free education to low-income families, has officially closed, impacting around 540 children who depended on its support. The Chan Zuckerberg Initiative, the school's benefactor, is redirecting its resources towards biotechnology and artificial intelligence. As part of its commitment, it has announced substantial funding aimed at assisting affected students and local organizations.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/mark-zuckerbergs-wife-priscilla-chan-invested-125-million-in-a-school-for-the-disadvantaged-now-she-is-closing-it-to-focus-on-ai/articleshow/132850734.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/mark-zuckerbergs-wife-priscilla-chan-invested-125-million-in-a-school-for-the-disadvantaged-now-she-is-closing-it-to-focus-on-ai/articleshow/132850734.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-04T13:36:24+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132850734,imgsize-74263.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Europe's shrinking rivers have hit shipping, power and tourism]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132852090.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Record low water levels in Europe's major rivers are disrupting electricity production, cargo transport and business operations as heatwaves and drought continue across the continent. Nuclear and hydropower plants have cut output, shipping on the Danube and Rhine has slowed, and companies are reporting lower earnings, highlighting the growing economic impact of prolonged extreme weather]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/europes-danube-rhine-and-loire-are-shrinking-under-heat-and-drought-disrupting-shipping-power-generation-and-tourism/articleshow/132852090.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/europes-danube-rhine-and-loire-are-shrinking-under-heat-and-drought-disrupting-shipping-power-generation-and-tourism/articleshow/132852090.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-04T13:45:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132852168,imgsize-192364.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Countries with most black mambas: From South Africa to Kenya, where the deadly snake is found]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132849672.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The black mamba, often cited as the most dangerous snake on the African continent, occupies a wide array of habitats. This snake thrives in arid savannas and rocky terrains throughout sub-Saharan Africa. Countries such as South Africa and Zimbabwe frequently report incidents of black mamba bites. Remarkably, sightings have increased in Kenya and Zambia at higher altitudes, with Tanzania and Botswana also within its expansive territory.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/countries-with-most-black-mambas-from-south-africa-to-kenya-where-the-deadly-snake-is-found/articleshow/132849672.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/countries-with-most-black-mambas-from-south-africa-to-kenya-where-the-deadly-snake-is-found/articleshow/132849672.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-04T14:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132849672,imgsize-57808.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Rose-ringed parakeets: From escaped pets to one of the most recognisable birds]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style=